## Turn state machine

`CPlayerAI` main vtable slot 0 = `0x0086DD40`. Its dispatcher at `0x0086DF40`: `ebx = [esi+0x128]`, `cmp ebx,0xE; ja`,
`jmp [ebx*4 + 0x0086E14C]`. Step names from `FUN_00866550`; slot 3 (`0x00866CF0`) returns the progress-bar value per step.

| # | Step | Handler | Main external callees |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | `INIT_DAY` | `0x00867440` (`CPlayerAI::SFLB_InitDay`, exported by H5X.exe) then `0x0086D750` | |
| 1 | `MOVE_HERO` | `0x0086B400` | `0x004B94B0`, `0x0068BD20`, `0x006BD7C0` |
| 2 | `COLLECT_PASSABLE_OBJECTS` | `0x00867520` | `0x004F6770`, `0x00C27740`, `0x00872620` |
| 3 | `BUILD_HERO_CHOICES` | `0x0086C760` | `0x00BD7110`, `0x00A37050` |
| 4 | `ESTIMATE_CHOICES` | `0x008667D0` | **`0x00872000`** (choice estimator) |
| 5 | `EXECUTE_BEST_CHOICE` | `0x0086C6B0` | `0x004E6C60`, `0x004E9A00` |
| 6 | `MANAGE_TOWNS` | `0x0086D4E0` | `0x00C283D0`, `0x009C5C60` |
| 7 | `HIRE_HEROES` | `0x0086B0A0` | `0x0098DE60`, `0x00C02A90` |
| 8 | `LAST_WAIT` | `0x00866700` | sets step 9 |
| 9 | `RETURN_TURN` | `0x00868EB0` | logs "end turn: %i steps, %i.%i seconds", ends the turn |
| 10 | `START_CHOOSE_DESTINATION` | `0x0086C570` | `0x00C27740`, `0x00872620`, `0x0063EE50` |
| 11 | `CHOOSE_DESTINATION` | `0x0086C010` | `0x00C07100`, `0x00C076D0`, `0x00C07AD0`, `0x00C07B20`, `0x00BCC020` |
| 12 | `MANAGE_HEROES` | `0x00869AD0` | `0x00BD7110`, `0x0074E870`, `0x00C5AF30` |
| 13 | `STEP_REARRANGE_TOWN_HEROES` | `0x00868CA0` | `0x0068BD20` |
| 14 | `STEP_ORDER_CARAVANS` | `0x0086A350` | `0x00CE6110`, `0x00CEA190` |

Step writes (`mov [reg+0x128], n`) are spread over the handlers above; `0x00868E00` (called after `SFLB_InitDay`)
sets the first step of the day.

## Destination candidates (`CHOOSE_DESTINATION`)

Call chain (all addresses verified in H5X.exe):

1. **`FUN_0086C010`** (step 11 handler) prepares the search on the global search object **`0x00FE8618`**
   (`0x00C07xxx` methods: `FUN_0086EF40` init, `FUN_00CEB670` start cell, `FUN_00C07AD0` / `C07B20` / `C07B60` /
   `C076C0` / `C07920` setup, `FUN_00C08BE0` = wave spread, timed → log `Wave spread: search limit = …`).
   Per-hero objects built before: `[CPlayerAI+0xC8] = FUN_00BC5B30(world, hero)` (**evaluator**, below) and
   `[CPlayerAI+0xD8] = FUN_00BCC020(world, hero)`. Then calls `FUN_00A7B630` at `0x0086C4EC`
   (also called from `FUN_008675F0` @ `0x008678E2`).
2. **`FUN_00A7B630` — selection loop.** Calls the builder, logs `found %i destinations` / `no destinations found`,
   optionally adds entries with `FUN_00A79700`, then scores each entry with `FUN_00A78940` and keeps the best
   (logs `new best` / `discarded, A <= B` / `discarded bonus …` / `discarded neutral for positive previous` via
   `FUN_00A7A0C0`). Ends with `no suitable destination found, search not finished` if nothing is better than staying.
3. **`FUN_00A7AF80` — candidate builder.** Walks the reachable points of the wave spread (`[0x00FE8618+0xDC]`,
   map grid at `+0xA8`). For each point: cost limits (`FUN_00A7C1D0` / `FUN_00A7C390`), map object at the point
   (`FUN_009D1570`, `0x00A7B224`), accessor slot `+0x00` non-null → skipped, **role filter `FUN_00A78400`**,
   dedup by object (keeps the cheaper path), skips owner-garrison and some `+0x54` cases, then calls
   **`FUN_00A78B60`** and **appends the entry (`FUN_00A7C940` @ `0x00A7B495`) only if its value is positive**:
   `0x00A7B46F call FUN_008664C0` (value > 0) or `FUN_00A78340` (cost ≥ 300 and "neutral" entry). **Candidates with a
   value ≤ 0 are dropped here without any log line.** At the end it also scores one more entry built from the hero's
   `+0x1C` object (role not identified).
   Entries are `0x48` bytes; value at `+0x08` (`int level; …; int64 amount` — compared level first), cost at `+0x18`.
4. **`FUN_00A78B60` — per-object filter + score.** Rejects the object if its interface accessor `+0x4C` is non-null,
   handles attractor/script targets, then calls the evaluator: `evaluator->vtable[0](entry+8, object, entry, cost)`.
   The large remaining block deals with owned/guarded/hero objects (battle simulations via `FUN_00BC3AF0`).
5. **Evaluator `NWorld::CEventValuePool`** (vtable `0x00E84E1C`, ctor `FUN_00BC5A80`, 0x40 bytes).
   Slot 0 **`FUN_00BC5740`**: cached value (`FUN_00BC5B80`) or the object's own AI estimator (object accessor
   `+0x6C` → sub-object `this-0x30`; estimator `+0x04` = applies to this hero, `+0x00` = value), else fallback
   **`FUN_00BC5480`**: switches the world to simulation (`+0x138/+0x13C`), measures the player's worth
   (`FUN_00872220`), applies the object to the hero (world `+0x74`), measures again → **value = worth after − before**.
   Then scripted attractors (`SetAIHeroAttractor`: ± `SearchPositive/NegativeAttractorValue`, 2 = level 3) and
   `FUN_00BC5710`.

### Role filter `FUN_00A78400` (`__thiscall`, ECX = object, EAX = hero)

Hero AI role = hero object vtable `+0x2BC` (log suffix: `Com`, `Fre`, `Col(<hero>)`, `Sup(<hero>)`).
- Role 1: accepts anything reachable this turn (cost ≤ move points); farther, only objects answering the hero `+0x2C`,
  town `+0x3C`, owner `+0x04`, pick-up `+0x20`, `+0x5C`, `+0x58` or monster `+0x1C` accessors (else `+0x28` → `+0x24`).
- Roles 2 / 3: within a Chebyshev distance taken from DefaultStats runtime offsets `+0x23C` / `+0x240` (same floor),
  otherwise mostly owner/ally-related objects.
- Any other role (incl. the main hero): accepts everything.

### Destination action types (`FUN_00A7A0C0`, by the target object's interface accessors)

Map objects expose an 80-slot interface-accessor vtable (each slot returns an interface pointer or 0):

| Accessor | Action name |
|---|---|
| `+0x2C` hero | `fight` (enemy) / `meet` / `meet ally` |
| `+0x38` ship | `fight hero aboard` / `meet in ship` / `meet ally in ship` / `enter` |
| `+0x1C` army (monster) | **`fight`** + stack name |
| `+0x20` pickable (artifact) | **`pick up`** |
| `+0x04` owner (flagged) | `capture` / `visit` / `visit ally` |
| none | `visit` |
| no object | `move to point`, `build ship in town`, `cast town portal and move`, `move and summon boat`, `move and dig`, `move and cast teleport` |

Other accessors seen: `+0x08` guards ("Creatures: …"), `+0x40` dwelling (creatures to purchase), `+0x48` shipyard
(dock), `+0x3C` town, `+0x6C` AI estimator. Concrete classes: `CAdvMapMonster` (accessor vtable `0x00E18F7C`,
answers `+0x08`, `+0x10`, `+0x1C`, `+0x28`, `+0x68`, `+0x6C`, `+0x70/+0x74`), `CAdvMapArtifact` (`0x00E187D4`,
answers `+0x20`), `CAdvMapTreasure` (`0x00E715EC`, resource piles / campfires, only common accessors → `visit`).

**Why the first log has no `fight` / `pick up` destination:** monsters and artifacts do answer `+0x1C` / `+0x20`, and
`+0x4C` is 0 for them, so they reach the evaluator; the remaining explanation is that their value is ≤ 0 and the
builder drops them at `0x00A7B46F`. To confirm it, `src/patches/AiLogs.cpp` hooks the second acceptance test
(`call FUN_00A78340` @ `0x00A7B480`, reached only when the value is not positive): when it also rejects the entry, the
game's destination logger `FUN_00A7A0C0` is called with the builder's own data (builder frame `B = esp` at the call:
entry `[B+0x4C]`, value `[B+0x54]`, hero main interface `[B+0x48]`, hero `[B+0xA0]`, 5th argument `[B+0xA8]`) →
rows tagged `destination (dropped, value <= 0)`. The per-class estimator (accessor `+0x6C`) of `CAdvMapMonster` was not identified yet
(no RTTI vtable at sub-object `+0x128`).

